# Kodus Extension Core Development Rules

## Code Style & Best Practices

- Avoid using try-catch blocks unless absolutely necessary for error handling
- Use async/await instead of promises when possible
- Prefer const over let, avoid var
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Write self-documenting code with clear variable names
- Keep functions small and focused on a single responsibility

## Extension Development Guidelines

- Always handle VSCode API calls properly
- Use proper activation events to optimize performance
- Implement proper cleanup in deactivate function
- Use vscode.window.showInformationMessage for user feedback
- Follow VSCode extension API guidelines
- Use proper error handling with user-friendly messages

## Testing

- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Test extension activation and deactivation
- Test all commands and their edge cases
- Use proper mocking for VSCode API calls

## Additional Rules

See other .cursor rules files for specific guidelines:
